WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
Last year, a country's
output was worth 800 billion.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.530
This year, it is worth 880 billion.

3
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.980
That is a rise of 10 per cent.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.170
Headlines cheer. Ministers smile.

5
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.190
But did the farms, factories
and shops really turn

6
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.720
out 10 per cent more?

7
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.820
More bread, more cars, more haircuts?

8
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.330
So if a country's output is
worth more money this year,

9
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.420
has it really produced more?

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.040
In this mission, you'll learn
exactly what GDP counts,

11
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.810
and what it leaves out.

12
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.820
Then you'll use a graph lab:

13
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.940
move two sliders and watch
two different measures of GDP.

14
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.860
Your mission: find out
when a bigger number means

15
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.760
a country truly made more.
